Once we have a hand-implemented merge like this, the risk becomes drift if new fields are added to the config. A unit-test that uses reflect to inspect the config struct that would detect new fields we'd need to merge and make us revisit the loader merge would probably be enough to mitigate that risk.

The other place we use mergo is more straightforward and could probably be updated to the latest version without any issues.
